  "lastName": "Czaja",
  "overview": "Dr. Wioletta Czaja (pronounced: chaya) is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Genetics, director of the Genetic and Genomic Sciences (GGSC) Undergraduate Program and associate scientist of the O’Neal Comprehensive Cancer Center. Dr. Czaja’s research investigates epigenetic and chromatin-based regulation of DNA repair and genome maintenance pathways in the context of cancer, inflammation and immune regulation. The long-term goal of our research is to uncover novel mechanisms of genome maintenance, and identify new targets for preventive and therapeutic strategies relevant to many types and stages of cancer and other diseases.",
